e power state if there is no previous value stored for Powered configuration, and this does not change the caching of power state after reboot.  BUT=chromium:731221 TEST=flash an image on a DUT and observe that Bluetooth is auto-enabled  Change-Id: Id8429d5b13dceff078528fd4a036eb4413e883f0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/540204 Commit-Ready: Rahul Chaturvedi &lt;rkc@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Rahul Chaturvedi &lt;rkc@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaturvedi &lt;rkc@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="540204" owner_email="mcchou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/bluez" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/bluez" ref="refs/changes/04/540204/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1040f5bc1b2fc4c58c87d8a2ce3f618edcf6f9b1" commit="be1686489cab4fa7af12bf74f50f2ec434b52713" commit_message="Limit types that can be read from guest memory  Not all types are safe to read from guest memory.  Any type with a reference or pointer will be initialized to random bits that don't refer to a valid address.  This can cause dangling pointer and general unsafe behavior.  To fix this, limit types that can be read with read_obj to those that implement the unsafe trait `DataInit`.  Provide implementations of `DataInit` for intrinsic types that are obviously safe to initialize with random data.  Implement the needed traits for bootparam types as they are read from the kernel image directly.  Change-Id: I1040f5bc1b2fc4c58c87d8a2ce3f618edcf6f9b1 Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/540750 Reviewed-by: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="540750" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" pro